       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 50 mg of amlodipine at once is in the range of a toxic ingestion, and I can't find a clinical scenario where it would be therapeutic. Repeating it daily would also be dangerous. The drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours, so it accumulates. The risks include profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and they would be hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose, or any lower dose you choose.\n- Add a second agent from another class if you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives you. I can enter that order too.\n- Enter nothing for now. If you have a protocol or special circumstance I don't know about, a pharmacist or the order-verification process can review it with you.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
